From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Rouesnel <wrouesnel@wrouesnel.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:15:43 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] rdp: Let a USB redirection broker handle URBDRC channels

RDP clients can redirect USB devices to the server over the URBDRC
dynamic virtual channel (MS-RDPEUSB). Implementing MS-RDPEUSB means
handling USB request blocks and making devices appear on the host. That
needs privileges and kernel interfaces that don't belong in
gnome-remote-desktop.

Leave that to a separate program, a USB redirection broker, and lend it
the session's URBDRC channels over a unix socket. When the session's
dynamic channels are ready, connect to the socket in the new
usb-redirection-socket setting, then open, close, and relay URBDRC
channel instances as the broker asks. gnome-remote-desktop doesn't
interpret any USB traffic.

docs/usb-redirection.md describes the socket protocol. The setting is
empty by default, which leaves USB redirection off. If nothing is
listening on the socket, the session carries on without it.
